        <obo:IAO_0000112>unable to assess for h/o exertional syncope, angina, dyspnea, etc which would warrant ICD placement</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement inferring that a finding/condition was assessed.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>It is anticipated that this relation will usually be negative (as seen in the example) and refer to the absence of an assessment for a particular condition.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4195693</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000028</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has assessment</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"assessed for pulmonary embolism" =&gt; has assessment
"evaluated for appendicitis" =&gt; has assessment
"screened for depression" =&gt; has assessment

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"unable to assess for syncope" =&gt; do not assert has assessment
"treated for pneumonia" =&gt; has intervention, NOT has assessment
"history of diabetes" =&gt; has finding, NOT has assessment

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient was assessed for pulmonary embolism."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "pulmonary embolism" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has assessment =&gt; TARGET
"She was evaluated for appendicitis."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "appendicitis" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has assessment =&gt; TARGET
"The patient was screened for depression."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "depression" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has assessment =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000030 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000030">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000006"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000104"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>stop Bactrim which may worsen hyperK</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any clinical justification or reason for ordering any intervention, including planning. If the reason is suspected, it would be qualified as uncertain.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4165917</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:416083004</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000030</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has reason</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"ordered because of hyperkalemia" =&gt; has reason
"started for treatment of pneumonia" =&gt; has reason
"discontinued due to adverse effects" =&gt; has reason

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"was caused by pneumonia" =&gt; is caused by, NOT has reason
"was recommended" =&gt; recommended, NOT has reason
"was suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT has reason

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"Bactrim was stopped because it worsened hyperkalemia."
SOURCE: "Bactrim" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "worsened hyperkalemia" =&gt; reason
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has reason =&gt; TARGET
"The MRI was ordered because of persistent headaches."
SOURCE: "MRI" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "persistent headaches" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has reason =&gt; TARGET
"Physical therapy was started to improve mobility."
SOURCE: "physical therapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "improve mobility" =&gt; reason
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has reason =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000031 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000031">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000113"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement related to patient physiologic state</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Was represented earlier as "finding related physiological patient state"</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4028872</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:128973006</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000031</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has state</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"patient is stable" =&gt; has state
"patient is improving" =&gt; has state
"patient is alert and oriented" =&gt; has state

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"stable disease" =&gt; has course, NOT has state
"chest pain" =&gt; has finding, NOT has state
"physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT has state

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient is clinically stable."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "clinically stable" =&gt; patient state
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has state =&gt; TARGET
"The patient is improving after treatment."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "improving" =&gt; patient state
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has state =&gt; TARGET
"The patient is alert and oriented."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "alert and oriented" =&gt; patient state
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has state =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000034 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000034">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000006"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000104"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000109"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Please call if we can be of further assistance or his echo is abnormal</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating that an intervention or task will be triggered by an event</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Referred by trigger criteria may be best fit.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:44787854</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:109721000000108</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000034</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has trigger</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"if fever develops, call the clinic" =&gt; has trigger
"abnormal results prompted admission" =&gt; has trigger
"worsening symptoms led to escalation" =&gt; has trigger

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"admission was caused by pneumonia" =&gt; is caused by, NOT has trigger
"admission was recommended" =&gt; recommended, NOT has trigger
"admission is suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT has trigger

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"If the fever returns, call the clinic."
SOURCE: "fever returns" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "call the clinic" =&gt; task
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has trigger =&gt; TARGET
"The abnormal CT result prompted admission."
SOURCE: "abnormal CT result" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "admission" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has trigger =&gt; TARGET
"Worsening hypoxia led to escalation of respiratory support."
SOURCE: "worsening hypoxia" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "escalation of respiratory support" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has trigger =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000035 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000035">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000006"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PHI presents today for follow-up evaluation regarding management of lower urinary tract symptoms.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Rationale for an outpatient visit</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Was previously "has visit reason" but the object was finding or intervention, not reason. Name was therefore changed to rationale to avoid confusion.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>LOINC:29298-7</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:3025141</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000035</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has visit rationale</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"visit for follow-up of lower urinary tract symptoms" =&gt; has visit rationale
"seen for evaluation of chest pain" =&gt; has visit rationale
"return visit for medication management" =&gt; has visit rationale

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"was referred by Dr. Smith" =&gt; is referred by, NOT has visit rationale
"was admitted to the ICU" =&gt; is admitted, NOT has visit rationale
"was treated with antibiotics" =&gt; has intervention, NOT has visit rationale

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient presented for follow-up of lower urinary tract symptoms."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "lower urinary tract symptoms" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has visit rationale =&gt; TARGET
"She was seen for evaluation of chest pain."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "chest pain" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has visit rationale =&gt; TARGET
"He returned for medication management."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "medication management" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has visit rationale =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000036 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000036">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000006"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>She had a MVC that resulted in extraperitoneal bladder injury and pelvic and sacral fractures.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement about the cause of a finding/condition</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>There is condition cause which is non-standard LOINC</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>LOINC:LP430632-2</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:1992175</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000036</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>is caused by</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"fracture caused by a fall" =&gt; is caused by
"dyspnea due to pneumonia" =&gt; is caused by
"bleeding secondary to anticoagulation" =&gt; is caused by

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"MRI ordered because of headache" =&gt; has reason, NOT is caused by
"possible pneumonia" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT is caused by
"fever preceded the rash" =&gt; precedes, NOT is caused by

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The fracture was caused by a fall."
SOURCE: "fracture" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "fall" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is caused by =&gt; TARGET
"The dyspnea was due to pneumonia."
SOURCE: "dyspnea" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is caused by =&gt; TARGET
"Bleeding was secondary to anticoagulation."
SOURCE: "bleeding" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "anticoagulation" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is caused by =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000037 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000037">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000006"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>She reports her catheter has been leaking today especially when trying to have a bowel movement.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating that procedure, intervention or finding/condition is complicated by an event</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Using complications, but not a relationship, may need new term.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4137797</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:263718001</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000037</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>is complicated by</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"wound complicated by infection" =&gt; is complicated by
"surgery complicated by bleeding" =&gt; is complicated by
"fracture complicated by nonunion" =&gt; is complicated by

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"infection caused the wound" =&gt; is caused by, NOT is complicated by
"surgery was followed by bleeding" =&gt; precedes, NOT is complicated by
"bleeding was suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT is complicated by

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The wound was complicated by infection."
SOURCE: "wound" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "infection" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is complicated by =&gt; TARGET
"The surgery was complicated by bleeding."
SOURCE: "surgery" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "bleeding" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is complicated by =&gt; TARGET
"The fracture was complicated by nonunion."
SOURCE: "fracture" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "nonunion" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is complicated by =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000038 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000038">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000006"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A diagnostic process outcome is consistent with a condition. Whether this process is required or sufficient is not addressed.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Was "Statement indicating that a diagnostic process does not suggest a finding/condition".</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000038</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>is consistent with diagnosis</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"imaging consistent with pneumonia" =&gt; is consistent with diagnosis
"biopsy consistent with malignancy" =&gt; is consistent with diagnosis
"findings consistent with appendicitis" =&gt; is consistent with diagnosis

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"imaging ruled out pneumonia" =&gt; negation, NOT is consistent with diagnosis
"biopsy suggested possible malignancy" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT is consistent with diagnosis
"MRI was ordered for headache" =&gt; has reason, NOT is consistent with diagnosis

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The CT findings were consistent with pneumonia."
SOURCE: "CT findings" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is consistent with diagnosis =&gt; TARGET
"The biopsy was consistent with malignancy."
SOURCE: "biopsy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "malignancy" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is consistent with diagnosis =&gt; TARGET
"The clinical findings were consistent with appendicitis."
SOURCE: "clinical findings" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "appendicitis" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is consistent with diagnosis =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000040 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000040">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000006"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A clinical reason related to a treatment such as procedure, medication, or lifestyle recommendation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000040</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>treatment reason</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"antibiotics for pneumonia" =&gt; treatment reason
"physical therapy to improve mobility" =&gt; treatment reason
"smoking cessation to reduce cardiovascular risk" =&gt; treatment reason

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"antibiotics caused diarrhea" =&gt; has effect, NOT treatment reason
"antibiotics were recommended" =&gt; recommended, NOT treatment reason
"antibiotics were suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT treatment reason

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"Antibiotics were prescribed for pneumonia."
SOURCE: "antibiotics" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; treatment reason =&gt; TARGET
"Physical therapy was ordered to improve mobility."
SOURCE: "physical therapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "improve mobility" =&gt; reason
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; treatment reason =&gt; TARGET
"Smoking cessation was advised to reduce cardiovascular risk."
SOURCE: "smoking cessation" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "reduce cardiovascular risk" =&gt; reason
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; treatment reason =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000041 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000041">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000005"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
