                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000104"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000105"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000107"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000111"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000108"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>I saw and evaluated the patient. I reviewed the findings and assessment/plan outlined above by PHI and agree</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement denoting a clinician's or patient's agreement with another clinician's assessment, recommendation or reasoning.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Mapping to "does agree with care plan".</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:37018830</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:714831004</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000041</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>agree with</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"agreed to proceed with surgery" =&gt; agree with
"concurred with the treatment plan" =&gt; agree with
"accepted the recommendation" =&gt; agree with

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"declined surgery" =&gt; negation or has decision, NOT agree with
"recommended surgery" =&gt; recommended, NOT agree with
"suspected pneumonia" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT agree with

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient agreed to proceed with surgery."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "surgery" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; agree with =&gt; TARGET
"The family concurred with the treatment plan."
SOURCE: "family" =&gt; family member; TARGET: "treatment plan" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; agree with =&gt; TARGET
"The patient accepted the recommendation."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "recommendation" =&gt; clinical decision
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; agree with =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000042 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000042">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000005"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Ultimately her goal is to not have to live with bilateral nephrostomy tubes.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Indication that an intervention or the patient has an outcome goal (target)</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>OMOP 4253630 "Goal"  doesn't really match well, we may need a new term.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4253630</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000042</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has goal</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"goal of pain control" =&gt; has goal
"target blood pressure below 130/80" =&gt; has goal
"aim of preventing recurrence" =&gt; has goal

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"reason for surgery" =&gt; has reason, NOT has goal
"recommended surgery" =&gt; recommended, NOT has goal
"completed treatment" =&gt; completed, NOT has goal

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The goal is pain control."
SOURCE: "intervention" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "pain control" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has goal =&gt; TARGET
"The target blood pressure is below 130/80."
SOURCE: "blood pressure management" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "below 130/80" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has goal =&gt; TARGET
"The aim is to prevent recurrence."
SOURCE: "treatment" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "prevent recurrence" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has goal =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000043 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000043">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000005"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000108"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Will discuss with interventional in AM about possible pulmonary vein dilation w/stenting</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A statement indicating that a clinician or patient has a decision concerning an intervention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>May needs new label, was previously has_pending_decision, but with modifieres this can be scoped more specifically.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000043</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has decision</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"decided to order an MRI" =&gt; has decision
"decision to start chemotherapy" =&gt; has decision
"will discuss surgical repair" =&gt; has decision

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"MRI was performed" =&gt; is performed by or completed, NOT has decision
"MRI was recommended" =&gt; recommended, NOT has decision
"MRI was suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT has decision

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The clinician decided to order an MRI."
SOURCE: "clinician" =&gt; clinician; TARGET: "order an MRI" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has decision =&gt; TARGET
"The team decided to start chemotherapy."
SOURCE: "team" =&gt; clinician; TARGET: "start chemotherapy" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has decision =&gt; TARGET
"The patient will discuss surgical repair."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "surgical repair" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has decision =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000044 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000044">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000005"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000105"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000106"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating that a finding/condition is at goal</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Goal achieved in SNOMED, rename if acceptable.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4191706</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:390802008</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000044</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>is at goal</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"at goal" =&gt; is at goal
"met the target" =&gt; is at goal
"reached the desired blood pressure" =&gt; is at goal

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"goal of pain control" =&gt; has goal, NOT is at goal
"worsening symptoms" =&gt; has course, NOT is at goal
"recommended target" =&gt; recommended, NOT is at goal

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient's blood pressure is at goal."
SOURCE: "blood pressure" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "at goal" =&gt; patient state
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is at goal =&gt; TARGET
"The treatment met the target."
SOURCE: "treatment" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "target" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is at goal =&gt; TARGET
"The patient reached the desired glucose level."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "desired glucose level" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is at goal =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000045 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000045">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000049"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000111"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement about documentation of a finding/condition</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Maps to SNOMED qualifier Reference documentation which is probably equivalent.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4205679</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:308910008</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000045</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>documentation of finding</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"the record documents hypertension" =&gt; documentation of finding
"the imaging report describes a mass" =&gt; documentation of finding
"the discharge summary notes anemia" =&gt; documentation of finding

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"the patient has hypertension" =&gt; has finding, NOT documentation of finding
"the patient underwent surgery" =&gt; has intervention, NOT documentation of finding
"the physician recommended treatment" =&gt; recommended, NOT documentation of finding

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The medical record documents hypertension."
SOURCE: "medical record" =&gt; documentation; TARGET: "hypertension" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; documentation of finding =&gt; TARGET
"The imaging report describes a pulmonary mass."
SOURCE: "imaging report" =&gt; documentation; TARGET: "pulmonary mass" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; documentation of finding =&gt; TARGET
"The discharge summary notes anemia."
SOURCE: "discharge summary" =&gt; documentation; TARGET: "anemia" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; documentation of finding =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000046 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000046">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating that the patient is a candidate for a given intervention, commonly used in the negative.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000046</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>is eligible</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"eligible for surgery" =&gt; is eligible
"eligible for transplant evaluation" =&gt; is eligible
"meets criteria for chemotherapy" =&gt; is eligible

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"contraindicated for surgery" =&gt; has contraindication, NOT is eligible
"referred for surgery" =&gt; is referred by, NOT is eligible
"scheduled for surgery" =&gt; has intention, NOT is eligible

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient is eligible for surgery."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "surgery" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is eligible =&gt; TARGET
"She meets criteria for transplant evaluation."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "transplant evaluation" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is eligible =&gt; TARGET
"He is eligible for chemotherapy."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "chemotherapy" =&gt; intervention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is eligible =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000048 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000048">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000049"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000108"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating that an intervention has been discussed with patient by a clinician (clinician initiated) or a patient has discussed an intervention with their clinician (patient initiated). The default assumption should be that the discussion is clinician initiated.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Likely need to break this down for reasoning, values available include separate concepts for discussion with caregiver, patient, specialist, pharmacist, payer, etc...</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000048</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>discussed with</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"discussed surgery with the patient" =&gt; discussed with
"reviewed chemotherapy with the family" =&gt; discussed with
"discussed the MRI with cardiology" =&gt; discussed with

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"recommended surgery" =&gt; recommended, NOT discussed with
"performed surgery" =&gt; completed, NOT discussed with
"referred to cardiology" =&gt; is referred by, NOT discussed with

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The surgeon discussed surgery with the patient."
SOURCE: "surgery" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "patient" =&gt; patient
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; discussed with =&gt; TARGET
"Chemotherapy was reviewed with the family."
SOURCE: "chemotherapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "family" =&gt; family member
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; discussed with =&gt; TARGET
"The MRI was discussed with cardiology."
SOURCE: "MRI" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "cardiology" =&gt; clinician
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; discussed with =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000049 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000049">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000003"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A decision or status has been confirmed.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4326761</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:74996004</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000049</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has confirmation</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"confirmed diagnosis" =&gt; has confirmation
"confirmed treatment plan" =&gt; has confirmation
"confirmed appointment" =&gt; has confirmation

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"suspected diagnosis" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT has confirmation
"recommended treatment" =&gt; recommended, NOT has confirmation
"denied symptoms" =&gt; negation, NOT has confirmation

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The diagnosis was confirmed."
SOURCE: "diagnosis" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "confirmed"
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has confirmation =&gt; TARGET
"The treatment plan was confirmed."
SOURCE: "treatment plan" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "confirmed"
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has confirmation =&gt; TARGET
"The appointment was confirmed."
SOURCE: "appointment" =&gt; task; TARGET: "confirmed"
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has confirmation =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000050 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000050">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>warfarin has contraindication pregnancy.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement about the contraindication of an intervention. The intervention should not be used for the condition because it may cause harm to the patient or outweigh potential benefits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4011945</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:103306004</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000050</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has contraindication</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"warfarin contraindicated in pregnancy" =&gt; has contraindication
"NSAIDs contraindicated in renal failure" =&gt; has contraindication
"chemotherapy contraindicated by severe neutropenia" =&gt; has contraindication

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"warfarin prescribed for atrial fibrillation" =&gt; has reason, NOT has contraindication
"chemotherapy was recommended" =&gt; recommended, NOT has contraindication
"chemotherapy was suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT has contraindication

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"Warfarin is contraindicated in pregnancy."
SOURCE: "warfarin" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "pregnancy" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has contraindication =&gt; TARGET
"NSAIDs are contraindicated in severe renal failure."
SOURCE: "NSAIDs" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "severe renal failure" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has contraindication =&gt; TARGET
"Chemotherapy is contraindicated because of severe neutropenia."
SOURCE: "chemotherapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "severe neutropenia" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has contraindication =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000051 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000051">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000105"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Her shortness of breath is becoming worse</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The course of a finding/condition</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>The same thing as clinical course.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4137632</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:263502005</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000051</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has course</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"worsening" =&gt; has course
"stable" =&gt; has course
"intermittent" =&gt; has course

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"three weeks" =&gt; has duration, NOT has course
"yesterday" =&gt; has date, NOT has course
"severe" =&gt; has severity, NOT has course

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient reports worsening weakness."
SOURCE: "weakness" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "worsening" =&gt; course
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has course =&gt; TARGET
"Her symptoms remain stable."
SOURCE: "symptoms" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "stable" =&gt; course
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has course =&gt; TARGET
"He has intermittent chest pain."
SOURCE: "chest pain" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "intermittent" =&gt; course
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has course =&gt; TARGET
"Bone density is decreasing."
SOURCE: "bone density" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "decreasing" =&gt; course
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has course =&gt; TARGET
"Cancer progression is rapid."
SOURCE: "cancer progression" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "rapid" =&gt; course
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has course =&gt; TARGET
A measurable property of a body site or disease process, such as "bone density" or "cancer
progression", is annotated as a single finding. Do not decompose it into the site plus the property;
there is no cue licensing such a relation, and CLCO has no observable entity class to hold the
property.</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000052 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000052">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000103"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>She has an appointment with Dr. PHI tomorrow</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Inference about the time when an event has happened or will happen</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>SNOMED attribute, qualifier is also available. Start and End dates?</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4256607</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:410671006</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000052</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has date</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"tomorrow" =&gt; has date
"on March 3" =&gt; has date
"last Tuesday" =&gt; has date

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"for three weeks" =&gt; has duration, NOT has date
"currently" =&gt; has temporal frame, NOT has date
"worsening" =&gt; has course, NOT has date

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient has an appointment tomorrow."
SOURCE: "appointment" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "tomorrow" =&gt; time
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has date =&gt; TARGET
"Surgery is scheduled for March 3."
SOURCE: "surgery" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "March 3" =&gt; time
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has date =&gt; TARGET
"The symptoms began last Tuesday."
SOURCE: "symptoms" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "last Tuesday" =&gt; time
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has date =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000053 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000053">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000103"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>She does endorse some nausea and spit up for the past two weeks</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating the duration of a finding/condition or intervention</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4014044</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000053</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has duration</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"for two weeks" =&gt; has duration
"lasting three months" =&gt; has duration
"over the past year" =&gt; has duration

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"yesterday" =&gt; has date, NOT has duration
"worsening" =&gt; has course, NOT has duration
"severe" =&gt; has severity, NOT has duration

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"She has had nausea for two weeks."
SOURCE: "nausea" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "for two weeks" =&gt; time
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has duration =&gt; TARGET
"The cough has lasted three months."
SOURCE: "cough" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "three months" =&gt; time
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has duration =&gt; TARGET
"Pain has persisted over the past year."
SOURCE: "pain" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "over the past year" =&gt; time
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has duration =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000054 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000054">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The patient underwent two kidney transplants (2002, 2012)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement of fact about a patient that constitutes past medical history</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>SNOMED CT United Kingdom clinical extension module sourced.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:44813766</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:722291000000108</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000054</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has history</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000055 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000055">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000025"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Patient mentioned genetic risk for DVT/PE from commercial DNA testing kit of unknown type</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating the patient is at risk for a condition or procedure.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:80943009</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000055</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has risk factor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A reified assertion relating two or more clinical entities, representing a contextualized clinical statement that can carry qualifiers such as negation, uncertainty, and temporality.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Although these structures represent relationships between clinical entities, we model them as reified associations rather than relations, because they represent contextualized assertions with additional attributes (e.g., negation, uncertainty, temporality), which cannot be expressed using binary object properties in OWL.
These relations include the most frequently documented relation types as defined in:
Colicchio, Tiago K., Pavithra I. Dissanayake, and James J. Cimino. "Formal representation of patients’ care context data: the path to improving the electronic health record." Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association 27, no. 11 (2020): 1648-1657.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>CLCO represents temporal information through four orthogonal mechanisms: (1) temporal_frame (qualifier axis) -- document-relative context via has_temporal_frame, values historical/current/future/hypothetical; (2) completion_status (qualifier axis) -- workflow state via has_completion_status, values pending/in_progress/completed; (3) datatype time properties (data axis) -- computable timestamps via has_start_time, has_end_time, has_duration_value with xsd typed literals; (4) reified temporal associations (entity axis) -- narrative temporal entities such as has_onset, has_date, has_duration where the temporal expression is a first-class clinical_entity linked via has_object. These mechanisms are independent: a single association may carry values from any combination.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000057</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>clinical association</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES: "The patient has pneumonia", "The MRI showed a mass", and "Surgery was recommended" are clinical associations.
NEGATIVE EXAMPLES: patient, pneumonia, and severe are entities or values, not associations by themselves.
CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: The first statement expresses a has finding association, the second a has finding association, and the third a recommendation association.</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000058 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000058">
        <owl:equivalentClass>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000107"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </owl:equivalentClass>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000107"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>He was given Zofran and meclizine at Urgent Care.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Inference about the location or setting where a clinical event happened.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:32462</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000058</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has setting</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"in the emergency department" =&gt; has setting
"at home" =&gt; has setting
"in the intensive care unit" =&gt; has setting

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT has setting
"tomorrow" =&gt; has date, NOT has setting
"physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT has setting

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient was treated in the emergency department."
SOURCE: "treated" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "emergency department" =&gt; setting
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has setting =&gt; TARGET
"The wound was managed at home."
SOURCE: "wound management" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "at home" =&gt; setting
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has setting =&gt; TARGET
"He was monitored in the intensive care unit."
SOURCE: "monitored" =&gt; task; TARGET: "intensive care unit" =&gt; setting
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has setting =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000060 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000060">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000067"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Modifies a relation to indicate that the relation is intended rather than actual. Presence-only: the axis has no value set, so the qualifier is either asserted or absent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Epistemic modality axis: captures whether the association describes an actual event or an intended/planned one. Orthogonal to temporal_frame (CLCO_0000082), which captures WHEN relative to the document, and completion_status (CLCO_0000063), which captures workflow state. An intended event may be past (we intended chemo but did not start), present, or future.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000060</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>intention</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"will start chemotherapy" =&gt; intention
"intended to undergo surgery" =&gt; intention
"plans to begin therapy" =&gt; intention
"scheduled for an MRI" =&gt; intention

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"underwent surgery" =&gt; completed, NOT intention
"recommended an MRI" =&gt; recommended, NOT intention
"may have pneumonia" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT intention
"had pneumonia last year" =&gt; historical, NOT intention

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient will start chemotherapy."
SOURCE: "chemotherapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "will start" =&gt; intention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has intention =&gt; TARGET
"The patient intended to undergo surgery."
SOURCE: "surgery" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "intended" =&gt; intention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has intention =&gt; TARGET
"She plans to begin physical therapy."
SOURCE: "physical therapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "plans to begin" =&gt; intention
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has intention =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000062 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000062">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000067"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The modified relationship is recommended, for example an intervention, admission or some action. Presence-only: the axis has no value set, so the qualifier is either asserted or absent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000062</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>recommended</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"recommended an MRI" =&gt; recommended
"should follow up" =&gt; recommended
"advised to stop smoking" =&gt; recommended
"the patient was told to rest" =&gt; recommended

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"underwent an MRI" =&gt; completed, NOT recommended
"will undergo surgery" =&gt; intention, NOT recommended
"may have pneumonia" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT recommended
"denied chest pain" =&gt; negation, NOT recommended

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The physician recommended an MRI."
SOURCE: "MRI" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "recommended" =&gt; recommended
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has recommended =&gt; TARGET
"The patient should follow up in two weeks."
SOURCE: "follow up" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "should" =&gt; recommended
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has recommended =&gt; TARGET
"She was advised to stop smoking."
SOURCE: "stop smoking" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "advised" =&gt; recommended
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has recommended =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000063 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000063">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000067"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The workflow completion state of a process. Orthogonal to temporal_frame (which captures when relative to the document) and intention (which captures intent). A process may be pending regardless of whether its temporal frame is past, present, or future.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Refactored from the original "status" class. Children include pending (moved from temporal), in_progress, and completed. Aligns with SNOMED procedure status qualifier values and EHR order status fields. No equivalent in NLP temporal annotation schemes like THYME or I2b2.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4138595</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:40642538</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000063</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>completion status</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"pending" =&gt; completion status
"in progress" =&gt; completion status
"completed" =&gt; completion status
"finished" =&gt; completion status

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"will undergo" =&gt; intention, NOT completion status
"recommended" =&gt; recommended, NOT completion status
"may undergo" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT completion status
"last year" =&gt; historical, NOT completion status

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The CT results are pending."
SOURCE: "CT results" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "pending" =&gt; completion status
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET
"The biopsy is in progress."
SOURCE: "biopsy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "in progress" =&gt; completion status
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET
"The procedure was completed."
SOURCE: "procedure" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "completed" =&gt; completion status
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000065 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000065">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000063"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>CT results pending</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process described by the association has been initiated (e.g., ordered, requested) but has not yet reached its terminal output state. This is a workflow status, not a temporal frame: a pending result may refer to a process that occurred in the past (e.g., labs drawn yesterday, results pending).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Moved from subClassOf temporal (CLCO_0000064) to subClassOf completion_status (CLCO_0000063). The previous definition conflated workflow state with temporal frame and epistemic modality. See temporal_plan.txt Section 1A for rationale.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:385645004</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000065</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>pending</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"results pending" =&gt; pending
"awaiting pathology" =&gt; pending
"order pending" =&gt; pending
"not yet resulted" =&gt; pending

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"procedure completed" =&gt; completed, NOT pending
"currently receiving therapy" =&gt; in progress, NOT pending
"will undergo surgery" =&gt; intention, NOT pending
"last year" =&gt; historical, NOT pending

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The CT results are pending."
SOURCE: "CT results" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "pending" =&gt; pending
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET
"The pathology report is still pending."
SOURCE: "pathology report" =&gt; documentation; TARGET: "pending" =&gt; pending
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET
"The laboratory order remains pending."
SOURCE: "laboratory order" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "pending" =&gt; pending
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000067 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000067">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A modifier that provides additional context to a clinical association, such as temporal frame, certainty, negation, or participant-level detail.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Renamed from "association qualifier" on 2026-10-20. The class names the qualifier axis only; what the qualifier scopes over is carried by the property used to attach it (has association qualifier, has subject qualifier, has object qualifier). The former name read as a commitment to statement scope, which the class does not make. Direct children are the six orthogonal axes.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000067</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>qualifier</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"suspected" =&gt; qualifier
"denied" =&gt; qualifier
"pending" =&gt; qualifier
"last year" =&gt; qualifier

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT qualifier
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT qualifier
"physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT qualifier
"three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT qualifier

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"A tumor was suspected."
SOURCE: "tumor" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "suspected" =&gt; qualifier
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET
"The patient denied fever."
SOURCE: "fever" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "denied" =&gt; qualifier
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET
"The results are pending."
SOURCE: "results" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "pending" =&gt; qualifier
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000068 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000068">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An association qualifier that modifies the entire clinical statement, such as intention, recommendation or completion status.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Obsoleted 2026-10-19. Qualifier scope is carried by the qualifier property, not by the qualifier class: has association qualifier (CLCO:0003000) attaches a qualifier to the whole association, has subject qualifier (CLCO:0003001) and has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002) attach it to a single participant. Encoding scope in the class hierarchy as well could not express the axis/scope cross-product -- negation (CLCO:0000080) and uncertainty (CLCO:0000081) were never subclasses of this class, so statement-scoped negation had no class to begin with. The class hierarchy now holds only the orthogonal qualifier axes. Former children intention (CLCO:0000060), recommended (CLCO:0000062) and completion status (CLCO:0000063) are now direct subclasses of association qualifier (CLCO:0000067); that they are statement-only is now asserted as the range of has participant qualifier instead.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:consider>CLCO:0003000</oboInOwl:consider>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000068</oboInOwl:id>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
        <rdfs:label>obsolete statement qualifier</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000069 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000069">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An association qualifier that modifies only the predicate (relationship type) of a clinical association, rather than the entire statement.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Obsoleted 2026-10-19. Qualifier scope is carried by the qualifier property, not by the qualifier class: has association qualifier (CLCO:0003000) attaches a qualifier to the whole association, has subject qualifier (CLCO:0003001) and has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002) attach it to a single participant. Encoding scope in the class hierarchy as well could not express the axis/scope cross-product -- negation (CLCO:0000080) and uncertainty (CLCO:0000081) were never subclasses of this class, so statement-scoped negation had no class to begin with. The class hierarchy now holds only the orthogonal qualifier axes. No instances were ever modelled and the class had no children. In a reified model the association node is anchored on the predicate itself, so a predicate-scoped qualifier is not distinguishable from a statement-scoped one during annotation. All three of its former contextual examples were in fact uncertainty, historical (CLCO:0000083) and negation, which already carry that guidance. Add a has predicate qualifier sub-property if a genuine predicate-scoped case is ever found.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:consider>CLCO:0003000</oboInOwl:consider>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000069</oboInOwl:id>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
        <rdfs:label>obsolete predicate qualifier</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000071 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000071">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A finding association specifying which facet, part, or functional dimension of an entity is being referred to in the assertion.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Obsoleted 2026-10-23. Every pattern this class was created for is expressible with existing vocabulary once the noun phrase is typed as a finding: "Bone density is decreasing" is has course (CLCO:0000051) over the finding "bone density"; "Cancer progression is rapid" is has course over "cancer progression", and course (CLCO:0000105) already lists "Rapidly progressing" among its own values; "Cardiac function is preserved" is has descriptive value (CLCO:0000075) over "cardiac function". All three have been moved to those classes. Four further reasons: the class had no cue -- every other association is licensed by a verb, preposition or connective, while aspect was licensed only by noun-noun juxtaposition, leaving no span to annotate; all three of its own contextual examples contradicted its own restrictions, using a finding site subject where finding was declared and a course object where value was declared; it shared the finding-to-value signature with has severity, has value, has descriptive value, has quantifiable value and now has laterality, adding no discriminating power; and its negative examples had to borrow has laterality and has spatial orientation to say what it was not. What aspect reached for -- density or function as a measurable property of a site -- is the SNOMED CT observable entity axis, which CLCO does not model. Should CLCO ever post-coordinate against LOINC, where the property axis is first class, or against SNOMED observable entities, that capability should return as an observable entity class on the clinical entity side, not as a finding-to-value association. Obsoleting this class does not foreclose it.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:consider>CLCO:0000051, CLCO:0000075, CLCO:0000024</oboInOwl:consider>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000071</oboInOwl:id>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
        <rdfs:label>obsolete has aspect</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000072 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000072">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000112"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The lesion is located on the anterior aspect of the left knee.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A finding association specifying the spatial orientation or anatomical direction of a finding relative to a body site.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Spatial orientation qualifiers reuse PATO quality terms directly; CLCO defines only the attachment role.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000072</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has spatial orientation</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"anterior to the knee" =&gt; has spatial orientation
"below the diaphragm" =&gt; has spatial orientation
"posterior to the heart" =&gt; has spatial orientation

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"left knee" =&gt; has laterality, NOT has spatial orientation
"severe pain" =&gt; has severity, NOT has spatial orientation
"three weeks" =&gt; has duration, NOT has spatial orientation

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The lesion is anterior to the knee."
SOURCE: "lesion" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "anterior to the knee" =&gt; finding site
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has spatial orientation =&gt; TARGET
"The mass is below the diaphragm."
SOURCE: "mass" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "below the diaphragm" =&gt; finding site
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has spatial orientation =&gt; TARGET
"The opacity is posterior to the heart."
SOURCE: "opacity" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "posterior to the heart" =&gt; finding site
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has spatial orientation =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000073 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000073">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000106"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Right-sided pneumothorax; bilateral knee pain.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A finding association specifying the laterality (left, right, bilateral, unilateral, or midline) of a finding. The object is the laterality value itself; the body site, where stated, is carried separately by has location.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Object changed from finding site (CLCO:0000112) to value (CLCO:0000106) on 2026-10-21. The previous restriction did not match the class's own examples: "left", "right-sided" and "bilateral" are laterality values, not body sites, whereas the sibling has spatial orientation (CLCO:0000072) genuinely does take a site ("anterior to the knee"). Where a site is also stated, express it separately with has location (CLCO:0000023).

Recorded alternative, not adopted: an earlier draft modelled this as a participant-scoped qualifier over PATO quality terms rather than as an association --

  laterality_qualifier
    ⊑ has_participant_qualifier only
       (PATO:0000611  # left
        or PATO:0000612  # right
        or PATO:0000613  # bilateral
        or PATO:0000614  # unilateral
        or PATO:0000610) # midline

That remains defensible: "left" in "left knee pain" modifies the knee, which is participant scope, and the draft would now use has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002). It was not adopted because the qualifier family is currently all-modal -- negation, certainty, temporal frame, completion status, intention, recommended -- and admitting a physical quality axis would mean widening the range of the participant properties, which is what encodes the restriction to scope-polymorphic modal axes. Revisit together with has spatial orientation, whose own note states the same PATO intent.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000073</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has laterality</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"left" =&gt; has laterality
"right-sided" =&gt; has laterality
"bilateral" =&gt; has laterality

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"anterior" =&gt; has spatial orientation, NOT has laterality
"severe" =&gt; has severity, NOT has laterality
"intermittent" =&gt; has course, NOT has laterality

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient has left knee pain."
SOURCE: "knee pain" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "left" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has laterality =&gt; TARGET
"A right-sided pneumothorax was seen."
SOURCE: "pneumothorax" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "right-sided" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has laterality =&gt; TARGET
"She has bilateral knee pain."
SOURCE: "knee pain" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "bilateral" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has laterality =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000074 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000074">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000057"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000106"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Severe abdominal pain; mild hearing loss.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A finding association specifying the severity or intensity of a finding or condition.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HP:0012824</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000074</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has severity</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"severe" =&gt; has severity
"mild" =&gt; has severity
"moderate" =&gt; has severity

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"worsening" =&gt; has course, NOT has severity
"left" =&gt; has laterality, NOT has severity
"for three weeks" =&gt; has duration, NOT has severity

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient has severe abdominal pain."
SOURCE: "abdominal pain" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "severe" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has severity =&gt; TARGET
"She reports mild hearing loss."
SOURCE: "hearing loss" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "mild" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has severity =&gt; TARGET
"He has moderate shortness of breath."
SOURCE: "shortness of breath" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "moderate" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has severity =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000075 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000075">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000024"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Patient describes dizziness as a room spinning sensation.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Information that qualitatively describes a finding, condition, or intervention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000075</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has descriptive value</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"room-spinning" =&gt; has descriptive value
"pressure-like" =&gt; has descriptive value
"nonproductive" =&gt; has descriptive value

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"38.5 degrees Celsius" =&gt; has quantifiable value, NOT has descriptive value
"headache" =&gt; finding, NOT has descriptive value
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT has descriptive value

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient described dizziness as room-spinning."
SOURCE: "dizziness" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "room-spinning" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has descriptive value =&gt; TARGET
"She described the pain as pressure-like."
SOURCE: "pain" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "pressure-like" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has descriptive value =&gt; TARGET
"The cough was nonproductive."
SOURCE: "cough" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "nonproductive" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has descriptive value =&gt; TARGET
"Cardiac function is preserved."
SOURCE: "cardiac function" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "preserved" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has descriptive value =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000076 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000076">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000024"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Blood pressure 130/80 mmHg; hemoglobin 10.2 g/dL.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Information that numerically quantifies a finding, condition, or intervention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>IAO:0000109</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000076</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>has quantifiable value</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"38.5 degrees Celsius" =&gt; has quantifiable value
"120/80 mmHg" =&gt; has quantifiable value
"10.2 g/dL" =&gt; has quantifiable value

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"severe" =&gt; has descriptive value or has severity, NOT has quantifiable value
"fever" =&gt; finding, NOT has quantifiable value
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT has quantifiable value

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The temperature was 38.5 degrees Celsius."
SOURCE: "temperature" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "38.5 degrees Celsius" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has quantifiable value =&gt; TARGET
"Blood pressure was 120/80 mmHg."
SOURCE: "blood pressure" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "120/80 mmHg" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has quantifiable value =&gt; TARGET
"Hemoglobin was 10.2 g/dL."
SOURCE: "hemoglobin" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "10.2 g/dL" =&gt; value
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has quantifiable value =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000077 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000077">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000006"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002501"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000111"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>The pink sputum suggests hemoptysis.</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A finding or condition suggested by a diagnostic process, documentation, another finding or condition, or an intervention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000077</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>suggests finding</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"imaging suggested pneumonia" =&gt; suggests finding
"the note raised concern for malignancy" =&gt; suggests finding
"the symptom pattern pointed to appendicitis" =&gt; suggests finding

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"imaging confirmed pneumonia" =&gt; is consistent with diagnosis, NOT suggests finding
"the patient denied pneumonia" =&gt; negation, NOT suggests finding
"MRI was ordered for headache" =&gt; has reason, NOT suggests finding

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The chest x-ray suggested pneumonia."
SOURCE: "chest x-ray" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; suggests finding =&gt; TARGET
"The note raised concern for malignancy."
SOURCE: "note" =&gt; documentation; TARGET: "malignancy" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; suggests finding =&gt; TARGET
"The symptom pattern pointed to appendicitis."
SOURCE: "symptom pattern" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "appendicitis" =&gt; finding
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; suggests finding =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000080 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000080">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000067"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>"Patient denies chest pain" (statement-level); "Tenderness is present, but not in the right upper quadrant" (participant-level).</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Signifies that the qualified element is negated. Applies at any scope: statement-level negation negates the entire association; participant-level negation negates a specific subject or object.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000080</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>negation</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"denied" =&gt; negation
"no evidence of" =&gt; negation
"without" =&gt; negation
"not present" =&gt; negation

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT negation
"recommended" =&gt; recommended, NOT negation
"completed" =&gt; completed, NOT negation
"severe" =&gt; value, NOT negation
"not always present" =&gt; do not negate the finding without checking scope

Negation cues must be interpreted with their scope. The word "not" alone does not always negate the clinical finding.

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient denied having a fever."
SOURCE: "fever" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "denied" =&gt; negation
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET
"No evidence of pneumonia was found."
SOURCE: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "no evidence" =&gt; negation
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET
"There was no fracture."
SOURCE: "fracture" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "no" =&gt; negation
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET

PARTICIPANT-SCOPED EXAMPLE:
"Tenderness is present, but not in the right upper quadrant."
SOURCE: "tenderness" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "not" =&gt; negation
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has object qualifier =&gt; TARGET
The finding is asserted and only its site is negated, so the negation attaches to the participant
filling the object slot. Using has association qualifier here would wrongly deny the tenderness.
Negation and uncertainty are the only two axes that may be attached at participant scope.</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000081 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000081">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000067"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>"The patient was possibly treated with antibiotics elsewhere" (statement-level: the treatment is what is uncertain); "Possible pneumonia was treated with antibiotics" (participant-level: the treatment happened, the diagnosis is uncertain).</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Signifies that the qualified element is uncertain or suspected. Applies at any scope: statement-level uncertainty qualifies the entire association; participant-level uncertainty qualifies a specific subject or object.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000081</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>uncertainty</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"suspected" =&gt; uncertainty
"possible" =&gt; uncertainty
"probable" =&gt; uncertainty
"may have" =&gt; uncertainty

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"denied" =&gt; negation, NOT uncertainty
"recommended" =&gt; recommended, NOT uncertainty
"completed" =&gt; completed, NOT uncertainty
"severe" =&gt; value, NOT uncertainty
"does not exclude" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT negation

"Does not exclude pulmonary embolism" indicates that pulmonary embolism remains possible; it does not assert that pulmonary embolism is absent.

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"A soft-tissue tumor was suspected."
SOURCE: "soft-tissue tumor" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "suspected" =&gt; uncertainty
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET
"CT findings suggested possible pneumonia."
SOURCE: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "possible" =&gt; uncertainty
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET
"The patient may have a pulmonary embolism."
SOURCE: "pulmonary embolism" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "may have" =&gt; uncertainty
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has association qualifier =&gt; TARGET

PARTICIPANT-SCOPED EXAMPLE:
"Possible pneumonia was treated with antibiotics."
SOURCE: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "Possible" =&gt; uncertainty
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has subject qualifier =&gt; TARGET
The treatment did happen and only the diagnosis is uncertain, so the uncertainty attaches to the
participant filling the subject slot. Using has association qualifier here would wrongly say the
treatment may not have happened. Negation and uncertainty are the only two axes that may be
attached at participant scope.</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000082 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000082">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000067"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The temporal location of the association relative to the moment of clinical documentation. Orthogonal to completion_status and intention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Replaces the deprecated temporal (CLCO_0000064). Aligns with THYME DocTimeRel and MedSpaCy temporal context flags. This axis answers WHEN relative to the document, not whether a process is complete (completion_status) or committed (intention).</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Currently statement-scoped only: this class is excluded from the range of has subject qualifier (CLCO:0003001) and has object qualifier (CLCO:0003002), unlike negation (CLCO:0000080) and uncertainty (CLCO:0000081), whose definitions state that they apply at any scope. This may be restructured as participant-scopeable depending on future time series work that will better integrate TimeML and DocTimeRel. The motivating pattern is a participant whose temporal frame differs from the association, for example "history of MI, now on aspirin", where the subject is historical but the association is current.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>biolink:temporal_context_qualifier</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000082</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>temporal frame</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"last year" =&gt; temporal frame
"currently" =&gt; temporal frame
"tomorrow" =&gt; temporal frame
"if symptoms recur" =&gt; temporal frame

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT temporal frame
"will start" =&gt; intention, NOT temporal frame
"pending" =&gt; completion status, NOT temporal frame
"suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT temporal frame

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient had pneumonia last year."
SOURCE: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "last year" =&gt; temporal frame
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"The patient will undergo surgery tomorrow."
SOURCE: "surgery" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "tomorrow" =&gt; temporal frame
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"If symptoms recur, restart treatment."
SOURCE: "restart treatment" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "if symptoms recur" =&gt; temporal frame
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000083 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000083">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000082"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Patient underwent two kidney transplants (2002, 2012)</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The association describes an event or state that occurred before the time of the clinical document.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>THYME:DocTimeRel_BEFORE</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000083</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>historical</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"last year" =&gt; historical
"previously" =&gt; historical
"history of" =&gt; historical
"in childhood" =&gt; historical

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"currently" =&gt; current, NOT historical
"tomorrow" =&gt; future, NOT historical
"may occur" =&gt; hypothetical, NOT historical
"pending" =&gt; pending, NOT historical

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient had pneumonia last year."
SOURCE: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "last year" =&gt; historical
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"She previously underwent surgery."
SOURCE: "surgery" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "previously" =&gt; historical
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"He has a history of diabetes."
SOURCE: "diabetes" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "history of" =&gt; historical
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000084 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000084">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000082"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Currently on metformin</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The association describes an event or state that overlaps with the time of the clinical document.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>THYME:DocTimeRel_OVERLAP</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000084</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>current</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"currently" =&gt; current
"now" =&gt; current
"at present" =&gt; current
"today" =&gt; current

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"last year" =&gt; historical, NOT current
"tomorrow" =&gt; future, NOT current
"if symptoms recur" =&gt; hypothetical, NOT current
"pending" =&gt; pending, NOT current

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient is currently on metformin."
SOURCE: "on metformin" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "currently" =&gt; current
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"The infection is present now."
SOURCE: "infection" =&gt; finding; TARGET: "now" =&gt; current
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"The patient is currently receiving therapy."
SOURCE: "receiving therapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "currently" =&gt; current
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000085 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000085">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000082"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Chemotherapy will begin next Tuesday</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The association describes an event or state that is expected to occur after the time of the clinical document.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>THYME:DocTimeRel_AFTER</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000085</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>future</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"tomorrow" =&gt; future
"next week" =&gt; future
"will begin" =&gt; future
"scheduled for next month" =&gt; future

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"last year" =&gt; historical, NOT future
"currently" =&gt; current, NOT future
"if symptoms recur" =&gt; hypothetical, NOT future
"pending" =&gt; pending, NOT future

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"Chemotherapy will begin next Tuesday."
SOURCE: "chemotherapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "next Tuesday" =&gt; future
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"The patient will undergo surgery tomorrow."
SOURCE: "surgery" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "tomorrow" =&gt; future
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"A follow-up visit is scheduled for next month."
SOURCE: "follow-up visit" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "next month" =&gt; future
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000086 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000086">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000082"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>If fever persists, start vancomycin</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The association describes a conditional or contingent event that may or may not occur depending on specified circumstances.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Sits at the boundary of temporal frame and modality. Placed under temporal_frame because NLP systems (THYME contextual_modality, MedSpaCy is_hypothetical) treat it as a document-context label at the same annotation layer as historical/current/future.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>THYME:contextual_modality_HYPOTHETICAL</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000086</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>hypothetical</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"if symptoms recur" =&gt; hypothetical
"should fever develop" =&gt; hypothetical
"in case of bleeding" =&gt; hypothetical
"could require admission" =&gt; hypothetical

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"last year" =&gt; historical, NOT hypothetical
"currently" =&gt; current, NOT hypothetical
"tomorrow" =&gt; future, NOT hypothetical
"completed" =&gt; completed, NOT hypothetical

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"If symptoms recur, restart treatment."
SOURCE: "restart treatment" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "if symptoms recur" =&gt; hypothetical
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"Should fever develop, call the clinic."
SOURCE: "call the clinic" =&gt; task; TARGET: "Should fever develop" =&gt; hypothetical
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET
"The patient could require admission."
SOURCE: "admission" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "could require" =&gt; hypothetical
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has temporal frame =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000087 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000087">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000063"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Antibiotics course ongoing</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process described by the association is actively executing but has not yet reached its terminal state.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000087</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>in progress</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"in progress" =&gt; in progress
"ongoing" =&gt; in progress
"currently receiving" =&gt; in progress
"underway" =&gt; in progress

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"pending" =&gt; pending, NOT in progress
"completed" =&gt; completed, NOT in progress
"will begin" =&gt; future or intention, NOT in progress
"last year" =&gt; historical, NOT in progress

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The antibiotic course is in progress."
SOURCE: "antibiotic course" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "in progress" =&gt; in progress
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET
"Physical therapy is ongoing."
SOURCE: "physical therapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "ongoing" =&gt; in progress
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET
"The patient is currently receiving chemotherapy."
SOURCE: "chemotherapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "currently receiving" =&gt; in progress
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000088 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000088">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000063"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Physical therapy completed</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process described by the association has reached its terminal output state.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000088</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>completed</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"completed" =&gt; completed
"finished" =&gt; completed
"performed" =&gt; completed
"concluded" =&gt; completed

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"pending" =&gt; pending, NOT completed
"in progress" =&gt; in progress, NOT completed
"will undergo" =&gt; intention or future, NOT completed
"may undergo" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT completed

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The biopsy was completed."
SOURCE: "biopsy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "completed" =&gt; completed
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET
"The procedure was performed."
SOURCE: "procedure" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "performed" =&gt; completed
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET
"Physical therapy has concluded."
SOURCE: "physical therapy" =&gt; intervention; TARGET: "concluded" =&gt; completed
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; has completion status =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A core clinical entity over which all clinical context associations occur.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>The 14 core clinical entity classes defined in:
Colicchio, Tiago K., Pavithra I. Dissanayake, and James J. Cimino. "Formal representation of patients’ care context data: the path to improving the electronic health record." Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association 27, no. 11 (2020): 1648-1657.
All of these should correspond to a subject or object in relations extracted by NLP systems. The exception to that is patient which may be inferred.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000100</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>clinical entity</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES: patient, chest pain, and appendectomy are clinical entities.
NEGATIVE EXAMPLES: has, severely, and because are a relation, modifier, and conjunction rather than clinical entities.
CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: In "The patient has chest pain", patient and chest pain are clinical entities; in "Appendectomy was scheduled", appendectomy is a clinical entity.</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000101">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A clinical finding of any type, including conditions, diagnosis and assessments.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Was finding/condition in original paper, can treat condition as a subclass if needed.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>biolink:DiseaseOrPhenotypicFeature</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000101</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>finding</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding
"Fever" =&gt; finding
"Headache" =&gt; finding
"Muscle weakness" =&gt; finding
"Shortness of breath" =&gt; finding


NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT finding
"Biopsy" =&gt; intervention, NOT finding
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT finding
"Mother" =&gt; family member, NOT finding
"Three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT finding
"Worsening" =&gt; course, NOT finding
"Severe" =&gt; value, NOT finding
"Suspected" =&gt; uncertainty, NOT finding


CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient presented with severe chest pain."
Annotate: "chest pain" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "severe" =&gt; value

"The patient reported progressively worsening muscle weakness."
Annotate: "muscle weakness" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "progressively worsening" =&gt; course

"MRI revealed a pulmonary nodule."
Annotate: "pulmonary nodule" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "MRI" =&gt; intervention

"The patient experienced intermittent headaches for three weeks."
Annotate: "headaches" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "intermittent" =&gt; course
Annotate: "three weeks" =&gt; time</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000102">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An intervention to treat or diagnose a finding/condition or the patient</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>There is not a SNOMED code for this as of 08/19/2026 documented in the athena ohdsi database.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>biolink:Procedure</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000102</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>intervention</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"MRI" =&gt; intervention
"Biopsy" =&gt; intervention
"Surgery" =&gt; intervention
"Antibiotic treatment" =&gt; intervention

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT intervention
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT intervention
"Three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT intervention
"Hospital" =&gt; setting, NOT intervention

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient underwent an MRI."
Annotate: "MRI" =&gt; intervention

"A biopsy was performed to evaluate the mass."
Annotate: "biopsy" =&gt; intervention
Annotate: "mass" =&gt; finding

"The patient started antibiotic treatment for pneumonia."
Annotate: "antibiotic treatment" =&gt; intervention
Annotate: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000103 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000103">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Numerical or narrative temporal data elements</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>Moved from subClassOf task (CLCO_0000109) to subClassOf clinical_entity (CLCO_0000100). Time is a first-class clinical entity type, not a subtype of task.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT:410669006</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000103</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>time</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Three weeks" =&gt; time
"Yesterday" =&gt; time
"Since childhood" =&gt; time
"For two months" =&gt; time

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT time
"Worsening" =&gt; course, NOT time
"Severe" =&gt; value, NOT time
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT time

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient has had headaches for three weeks."
Annotate: "headaches" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "three weeks" =&gt; time

"The symptoms began yesterday."
Annotate: "symptoms" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "yesterday" =&gt; time

"The patient has experienced pain since childhood."
Annotate: "pain" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "since childhood" =&gt; time</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000104 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000104">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Justifications and reasons for ordering, performing, planning, or discontinuing an intervention or diagnostic process</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>SNOMEDCT sourced from Athena OHDSI "Reason and justification" (https://athena.ohdsi.org/search-terms/terms/4128496)</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT:288830005</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000104</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>reason</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Because of worsening pain" =&gt; reason
"History of diabetes" =&gt; reason
"Abnormal imaging result" =&gt; reason
"Patient preference" =&gt; reason

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT reason
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT reason
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT reason
"Three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT reason

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The MRI was ordered because of persistent headaches."
Annotate: "MRI" =&gt; intervention
Annotate: "persistent headaches" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "because of persistent headaches" =&gt; reason

"Surgery was postponed due to the patient's cardiac risk."
Annotate: "surgery" =&gt; intervention
Annotate: "cardiac risk" =&gt; reason</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000105 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000105">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Course of a finding/condition</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT:260908002</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000105</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>course</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Stable" =&gt; course
"Worsening" =&gt; course
"Intermittent" =&gt; course
"Rapidly progressing" =&gt; course

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Two weeks" =&gt; time, not course
"sudden onset" =&gt; time, not course


CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient reported progressively worsening weakness."
Annotate: "progressively worsening" =&gt; course
Annotate: "weakness" =&gt; finding

"The patient's symptoms have remained stable."
Annotate: "stable" =&gt; course

"The patient experienced intermittent episodes of chest pain."
Annotate: "intermittent" =&gt; course</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000106 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000106">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any numerical or narrative description of a finding/condition or intervention</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>SNOWMEDCT code for "hasvalue" sourced from Athena OHDSI database (https://athena.ohdsi.org/search-terms/terms/4306768)</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOWMEDCT:83568003</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000106</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>value</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"38.5 degrees Celsius" =&gt; value
"120/80 mmHg" =&gt; value
"Positive" =&gt; value
"No improvement" =&gt; value

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Fever" =&gt; finding, NOT value
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT value
"Three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT value

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient's temperature was 38.5 degrees Celsius."
Annotate: "temperature" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "38.5 degrees Celsius" =&gt; value

"The CT result was positive for pneumonia."
Annotate: "CT" =&gt; intervention
Annotate: "positive" =&gt; value
Annotate: "pneumonia" =&gt; finding</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000107 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000107">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Health care setting or location</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>There is not a SNOMED code for this as of 08/19/2026 documented in the athena ohdsi database.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000107</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>setting</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Emergency department" =&gt; setting
"Intensive care unit" =&gt; setting
"Outpatient clinic" =&gt; setting
"Home" =&gt; setting

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT setting
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT setting
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT setting
"Three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT setting

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient was admitted to the intensive care unit."
Annotate: "patient" =&gt; patient
Annotate: "intensive care unit" =&gt; setting

"The procedure was performed in the outpatient clinic."
Annotate: "procedure" =&gt; intervention
Annotate: "outpatient clinic" =&gt; setting</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000108 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000108">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Health care professional, unlike SNOMED, includes only people working directly with patients such as physicians, nurses, etc... Administrative healthcare professionals such as healthcare billing coders are not included.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT:44804106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000108</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>clinician</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Physician" =&gt; clinician
"Nurse practitioner" =&gt; clinician
"Physician assistant" =&gt; clinician
"Radiologist" =&gt; clinician
"Pathologist" =&gt; clinician
"Pharmacist" =&gt; clinician

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Mother" =&gt; family member, NOT clinician
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT clinician
"30-year-old male patient" =&gt; patient, NOT clinician</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000109 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000109">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any healthcare related task not related to direct clinical activities (e.g., phone call or uploading a medical record file).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>SNOMEDCT code sourced from Athena OHDSI "TASK" (https://athena.ohdsi.org/search-terms/terms/4008963)</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT:101878003</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000109</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>task</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Phone call" =&gt; task
"Uploading a medical record" =&gt; task
"Scheduling an appointment" =&gt; task
"Reviewing the chart" =&gt; task

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT task
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT task
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT task
"Emergency department" =&gt; setting, NOT task

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The nurse called the patient to confirm the appointment."
Annotate: "nurse" =&gt; clinician
Annotate: "called the patient" =&gt; task

"The staff uploaded the medical record to the portal."
Annotate: "uploaded the medical record" =&gt; task
Annotate: "medical record" =&gt; documentation</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The patient entity</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT:116154003</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>biolink:Case</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000110</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>patient</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"The patient" =&gt; patient
"The 30-year-old man" =&gt; patient
"The child" =&gt; patient
"She" =&gt; patient, when the clinical note clearly identifies the referent as the patient

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT patient
"Mother" =&gt; family member, NOT patient
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT patient
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT patient

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient reported chest pain."
Annotate: "patient" =&gt; patient
Annotate: "chest pain" =&gt; finding

"She underwent surgery for a fractured femur."
Annotate: "She" =&gt; patient
Annotate: "surgery" =&gt; intervention
Annotate: "fractured femur" =&gt; finding</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000111 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000111">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Clinical documentation, e.g., progress notes, imaging reports</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>IAO:0000310</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000111</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>documentation</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112/><obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Medical Record" =&gt; documentation
"Discharge summary" =&gt; documentation
"Patient chart" =&gt; documentation
"Clinical note" =&gt; documentation

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT documentation
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT documentation
"Three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT documentation
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT documentation
"Worsening" =&gt; course, NOT documentation

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:

"The medical record noted a history of hypertension."
Annotate: "medical record" =&gt; documentation
Annotate: "hypertension" =&gt; finding

"According to the clinical notes, the patient underwent surgery."
Annotate: According to the "clinical notes" =&gt; documentation
Annotate: "surgery" =&gt; intervention</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000112 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000112">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Anatomical site of a finding/condition</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:123037004</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UBERON:0001062</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000112</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>finding site</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Chest" =&gt; finding site
"Cervical spine" =&gt; finding site
"Pituitary" =&gt; finding site
"Ovary" =&gt; finding site

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT finding site as a whole
"Headache" =&gt; finding, NOT finding site
"Swelling" =&gt; finding, NOT finding site
"MRI" =&gt; intervention, NOT finding site

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:

"The patient reported pain in the left knee."
Annotate: "pain" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "left knee" =&gt; finding site

"The patient presented with swelling of the right ankle."
Annotate: "swelling" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "right ankle" =&gt; finding site

"CT revealed a mass in the left lung."
Annotate: "mass" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "left lung" =&gt; finding site
Annotate: "CT" =&gt; intervention

"The patient experienced tenderness over the lower abdomen."
Annotate: "tenderness" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "lower abdomen" =&gt; finding site

"The patient had a fracture of the left femur."
Annotate: "fracture" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "left femur" =&gt; finding site

"MRI demonstrated a lesion in the right temporal lobe."
Annotate: "lesion" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "right temporal lobe" =&gt; finding site
Annotate: "MRI" =&gt; intervention</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000113 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000113">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Patient state, e.g., stable, improving. The overall patient state, not whether a particular disease or condition is stable or improving.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>SNOMEDCT was sourced from Athena OHDSI "Patient Status" (http://athena.ohdsi.org/search-terms/terms/4077556)</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOWMEDCT:246097001</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000113</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>patient state</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Stable" =&gt; patient state
"Improving" =&gt; patient state
"Unstable" =&gt; patient state
"Alert and oriented" =&gt; patient state

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Stable disease" =&gt; course, NOT patient state
"Chest pain" =&gt; finding, NOT patient state
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT patient state
"Three weeks" =&gt; time, NOT patient state

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient is clinically stable."
Annotate: "patient" =&gt; patient
Annotate: "clinically stable" =&gt; patient state

"The patient is improving after treatment."
Annotate: "patient" =&gt; patient
Annotate: "improving" =&gt; patient state
Annotate: "treatment" =&gt; intervention

"The patient's symptoms are stable."
Annotate: "symptoms" =&gt; finding
Annotate: "stable" =&gt; course</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000114 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000114">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000058"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0002502"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000110"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>Patient discharged this morning with family</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Statement indicating that the patient has been discharged from a clinical setting</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>OMOP_CONCEPT_ID:4137031</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:58000006</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000114</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>is discharged</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"discharged home" =&gt; is discharged
"discharged from the hospital" =&gt; is discharged
"ready for discharge" =&gt; is discharged

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"admitted to the hospital" =&gt; is admitted, NOT is discharged
"transferred to rehabilitation" =&gt; is transferred to, NOT is discharged
"referred to cardiology" =&gt; is referred by, NOT is discharged

CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient was discharged home."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "home" =&gt; setting
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is discharged =&gt; TARGET
"She was discharged from the hospital."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "hospital" =&gt; setting
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is discharged =&gt; TARGET
"He is ready for discharge."
SOURCE: "patient" =&gt; patient; TARGET: "discharge" =&gt; clinical administration
RELATION: SOURCE =&gt; is discharged =&gt; TARGET</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000115 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000115">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLCO_0000100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A person who is a member of the patient's family. A caregiver who is not a family member would be identified as a clinician.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMED:303071001</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>CLCO:0000115</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>family member</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES:
"Mother" =&gt; family member
"Father" =&gt; family member
"Sister" =&gt; family member
"Brother" =&gt; family member
"Daughter" =&gt; family member

NEGATIVE EXAMPLES:
"Patient" =&gt; patient, NOT family member
"Physician" =&gt; clinician, NOT family member
"Nurse practitioner" =&gt; clinician, NOT family member


CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES:
"The patient's mother has a history of breast cancer."
Annotate: "mother" =&gt; family member
Annotate: "breast cancer" =&gt; finding

"His father was diagnosed with diabetes."
Annotate: "father" =&gt; family member
Annotate: "diabetes" =&gt; finding

"The patient's sister reported similar symptoms."
Annotate: "sister" =&gt; family member</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A generically dependent continuant that is about some entity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>information content entity</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000112>POSITIVE EXAMPLES: a clinical statement, MRI report, and discharge summary are information content entities.
NEGATIVE EXAMPLES: patient, pneumonia, and an MRI machine are respectively a clinical entity, finding, and physical object.
CONTEXTUAL EXAMPLES: In "The report states that the patient has pneumonia", the report is an information content entity; MRI report and discharge summary function similarly.</obo:IAO_0000112></owl:Class>
    


